      "writtenOn": "2020-04-22T18:20:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t it needs to be unmasked. We unmask the VBUS presence interrupt (which is gated by CONFIG_USB_PD_VBUS_DETECT_TCPC), so that\u0027s the event that is triggering this. The TCPCI spec says that \"[The VBUS presence] bit is not valid when POWER_STATUS.VbusDetectionEnabled\n\u003d 0b.\" hence why I\u0027m checking that.\n\nIt\u0027s not immediately clear to me why one would want to mask/unmask the VBUS detection interrupt; it\u0027s enabled by default and the TCPM turns it off with an explicit command. VBUS presence makes sense, but VBUS detection enabled/disabled makes less sense in my opinion.",
